      <room>H.1308</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Debian GNU/kFreeBSD</title>
      <subtitle>apt-get install freebsd?</subtitle>
      <track>CrossDistro devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk will show you what Debian GNU/kFreeBSD exactly is, what the&#xA;  differences between Debian GNU/kFreeBSD and the well known Debian&#xA;  GNU/Linux are, what difficulties the developers had, especially with&#xA;  regards to packaging and infrastructure, and what design decisions&#xA;  where made to get so far that Debian GNU/kFreeBSD finally has been&#xA;  accepted as Debian release architecture and what you can do with it&#xA;  but not with Debian GNU/Linux or with plain FreeBSD.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It&amp;#39;s also gives a&#xA;  little overview over similar projects. (There are more than you may&#xA;  expect. :-)&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="651">Axel Beckert</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>